    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings without obstruction.\n• Mark or label the rear access point so responders can locate it quickly without searching.\n• Keep the rear access gate unlocked or secured with a breakaway latch to allow responders to enter without delay.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area clear of stored items so arriving units have room to stage and turn around.\n• Trim any landscaping along the walkway that could slow or block responder movement to the front entry.\n• Mark utility shutoffs in the utility area with clearly visible labels so responders can locate them without assistance.\n• Post the property address at both the street and at the detached structure if it is not visible from the driveway approach.\n• Keep the patio area clear of furniture or stored items that could block movement around the exterior of the residence.\n• Confirm that fenced sections have at least one gate wide enough for responders carrying equipment to pass through."
